Paste clipboard images into terminals as uploaded file paths.

A browser terminal can't hand a clipboard image to a CLI: Claude Code and
Codex read images from the clipboard of the machine they run on, and inside
the container there is none. This catches paste events whose clipboard holds
only images, uploads each one through Freshell's existing authenticated
attachments endpoint (POST /api/fresh-agent/attachments, saved under
~/.freshell/attachments), and pastes the saved path(s) as a bracketed paste,
which Claude Code and Codex attach as images. Clipboards that also carry text
paste as text, unchanged.

